00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:05.260
Leah: Early computer codes date back
to the 19th Century and many modern

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:09.889
programming languages stem from 'Ada
Lovelace's first machine algorithm'

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:15.120
which was developed for Charles
Babbage's Difference machine in 1843.

00:00:16.029 --> 00:00:20.240
It was the 1940's that the first modern
computers were created along with

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:22.419
machine-specific assembly language.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:27.909
However, it was the 1950's that the first
modern programming language was born.

00:00:28.439 --> 00:00:31.410
This was FORTRAN short
for formula translator.

00:00:32.179 --> 00:00:33.580
Others were to follow such as

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:34.859
LISP - list processor,

00:00:34.859 --> 00:00:37.230
ALGOL -algorithmic language

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.879
and COBOL -common
business-oriented language.

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:44.950
In the 1960's BASIC had been
invented and then C was released.

00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:50.095
Unix was developed in the 1970’s
and it’s code rewritten in ‘C’ in

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:55.489
1972, the first major OS or operating
system not in assembly language.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:01.239
Linux first released in 1991 is
written almost entirely in C and both

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:04.300
Windows and macOS both contain C.

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:10.429
The 1990’s also welcomed some of today’s
most recognisable languages such as

00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:13.920
Python, Java, Java Script and PHP.

00:01:14.410 --> 00:01:19.770
Which opened the world to social media,
Android/OS apps and streaming services.

00:01:20.429 --> 00:01:24.210
To learn more, take a look at the
website further down on this page…

